  "respell": {
    "_doc": [
      "The spellings the generator gives every name it emits once the words above have named it, the overlay's own names included",
      "(ZabbixRespellings): records, fields, enums and their members, and each object's client and property. A name keeps no",
      "abbreviation (Microsoft's general naming conventions: GetWindow, not GetWin) and writes a two-letter acronym in capitals (the",
      "capitalization conventions' IOStream), so EvalType is EvaluationType, Ip is IP, and Username is the conventions' UserName.",
      "Applied once, after the names above, so the records, the clients, the cmdlet parameters and the views see one name; a",
      "command's noun stays the one its object had before (the modules keep their commands). parts: a capitalised part of a name",
      "wherever it stands (OkAckColor is OkAcknowledgedColor, ZabbixHaNodeClient is ZabbixHANodeClient); no generated name keeps a",
      "key of it (DesignConformanceTests.Names). names: a whole name the parts would leave unclear, taken before them (a host's",
      "TechnicalName is its HostName, a media type's ExecPath its ScriptName). fields: a field named after its wire where its type",
      "says more, keyed by its name and kind (a host's flags are its DiscoveryKind), or by its record and name where the same name",
      "means another thing elsewhere (item.get's host is a HostName; a user directory's host is the LDAP server's). taken: the name",
      "a field takes where its respelling is another field's already (an item's params are its TypeParameters: its parameters are",
      "a script item's named parameters)."
    ],
